#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087459 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "dfbe689c-ae04-5405-9a38-d80f10662a0b" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Equation of a Horizontal Hyperbola in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "dad615d8-1f62-51a0-aa21-b93313e1bfbf" :question/math-academy-id "e-5117" :question/problem "Write the equation of the hyperbola $9 x^2 - 16y^2 = 144$ in standard form." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{x^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{y^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $144$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n9x^{2} - 16y^{2} &= 144 \\\\\n\\frac{9x^{2}}{144} - \\frac{16y^{2}}{144} &= \\frac{144}{144} \\\\\n\\frac{x^{2}}{16} - \\frac{y^{2}}{9} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186087550 :knowledge-point/_canonical-example [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9f783fe8-8f52-5f93-adef-bf4bd030fea0" :knowledge-point/title "Writing the Equation of a Vertical Hyperbola in Standard Form"}] :question/id #uuid "93259130-d7bd-5db7-9bd5-c83c80ceb874" :question/math-academy-id "e-6774" :question/problem "Write the equation of the hyperbola $4y^2-7x^2=84$ in standard form." :question/worked-solution "The Cartesian equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at the origin is\n\n$$\n\\frac{y^2}{a^2} - \\frac{x^2}{b^2}=1\n$$\n\nTherefore, to write the equation of the hyperbola in standard form, we need to divide both sides of the equation by $84$ and then simplify, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\n4y^{2} - 7x^{2} &= 84 \\\\\n\\frac{4y^{2}}{84} - \\frac{7x^{2}}{84} &= \\frac{84}{84} \\\\\n\\frac{y^{2}}{21} - \\frac{x^{2}}{12} &= 1\n\\end{aligned}\n$$"}]}
